## Conclusions

It is a pity that in Chile you must go into supreme-level debt in order to study. People are practically forced to study outside the country or simply be self-taught to avoid the abusive student loans.

So, mechón or mechona (Chilean slang for freshman) who wants to study computer science at a university in Chile. My humble recommendation is that you study a 6 to 12 month course on Frontend, build a good project portfolio and get a well-paid job fast. First invest in improving your skills and then when you have a good salary you can study at the University if you want, without going into debt.

In any case, despite all the difficulties
you should still study something formal if you can and not just stay
with youtube videos or bootcamps. The university
gives new experiences and possibly makes you grow
beyond your limits.
